{"Inconsistent error response format between the two 422 paths: the non-list-data case returns an empty Response(status=422) while the validation-failure case returns a JSON body. Both should use the same format.": 0.29409539699554443, "zip(error_ids, events.values()) assumes the dict returned by get_multi preserves the input order of node_ids, but get_multi reorders entries when some are served from cache (uncached items first, then items.update(cache_items) appends cached ones). This silently pairs error IDs with wrong event data.": 0.9787735342979431, "Hidden attributes are only filtered when the user is actively searching. When searchQuery is empty, the early return on the previous line returns sorted without filtering out HIDDEN_ATTRIBUTES, so is_segment, project_id, and received will still be visible by default.": 0.9857935309410095, "TableWidgetVisualization is rendered with hardcoded empty columns and tableData, discarding the actual query results (result.data, result.meta, fields) that are available in scope. Anyone enabling the use-table-widget-visualization feature flag will see blank tables.": 0.994098424911499, "projectIds is a new array reference every render (when projects is provided), defeating the downstream useMemo/useCallback dependency checks and causing unnecessary query refetches. Wrap it in useMemo.": 0.6785299777984619, "Same truthiness bug as in validate_timestamp: self.initial_data.get('timestamp') returns 0 (falsy) when timestamp=0, which is a valid value per min_value=0. Use 'timestamp' in self.initial_data instead.": 0.9885461926460266, "Truthiness check on self.initial_data.get('age') fails for falsy values like 0. Since age and timestamp are integers, a value of 0 is falsy in Python and would bypass this mutual exclusivity validation. Use 'age' in self.initial_data to check for key presence instead.": 0.9914290308952332, "processing_deadline_duration=120 (2 min) is shorter than the task's internal BATCH_SCHEDULE_OFFSET deadline of 180 seconds (3 min). The task will be killed by the worker before it can exit gracefully via its own deadline check, potentially interrupting mid-delivery.": 0.6691315770149231, "The OAuth state parameter is set to pipeline.signature, which appears to be a deterministic pipeline-derived value rather than a per-request cryptographic random nonce. RFC 6749 \u00a710.12 recommends the state be an unpredictable per-request value bound to the user's session to effectively prevent CSRF during OAuth flows.": 0.008902657777071, "integration.metadata['sender'] will raise a KeyError if the sender key was never populated. In build_integration(), sender is only added to metadata when state.get('sender') is truthy. Use .get() with a safe fallback to avoid crashing the installation flow.": 0.0065015931613743305, "Using transparent (which is rgba(0,0,0,0)) instead of a zero-alpha version of the background color causes a dark band in the gradient when the theme background isn't black. The LeftMask already handles this correctly with Color(p.theme.background).alpha(0).rgb().string() \u2014 the RightMask should match.": 0.9905059933662415, "summary can be null (per the hook's return type), but the component doesn't guard against it. If the API returns a successful response with a null summary, the UI will render the 'Feedback Summary' header and icon with an empty content area. Add a null/empty check before rendering.": 0.9814444780349731, "Replacing FlexCenter with Flex drops the overflow: hidden (from overflowEllipsis) that the old styled component had. Because this element is a CSS-grid item, it needs overflow: hidden or min-width: 0 to allow the cell to shrink below its content width \u2014 otherwise long file names will overflow instead of showing an ellipsis.": 0.9428791403770447, "The migration from FlexBox to Flex drops height: 100%. The old styled component explicitly set height: 100%, which is not replicated by any prop on the Flex component. This could cause layout regression in contexts where the parent doesn't stretch children via flex.": 0.9630324840545654, "The useCallback dependency includes the entire selection object, but only selection.datetime and selection.projects are used in the callback body. This causes unnecessary re-creation of the callback (and downstream re-renders) whenever unrelated page filter state like environments changes.": 0.2913786470890045, "Analytics event is recorded before the feature flag check, so requests that are rejected due to the feature being disabled will still be tracked. Move analytics.record() after the features.has() guard to avoid polluting analytics data with rejected requests.": 0.9844862222671509, "Missing align='center' and gap={space(1)} \u2014 the old FlexBox had both. The three placeholder items will lose their vertical centering and spacing.": 0.8976483941078186, "Missing align='center' and gap={space(1)} \u2014 the old Container inherited these from FlexBox. This will cause a visual regression (tabs and vitals won't be vertically centered and will lose their gap).": 0.9190284013748169, "name is typed as TFields but represents a display label, not a field key. When TabularColumn is instantiated with a specific field union, name is restricted to those literal keys, preventing friendly display names like 'Average'. Consider typing name as string.": 0.4024503529071808, "SummaryListContainer is missing min-height: 0 (or overflow: hidden). As a CSS Grid item in a 1fr row, it defaults to min-height: auto, which prevents it from shrinking below its content. This breaks the scroll behavior of the inner FeedbackList.": 0.8952014446258545, "The _handle_regex_match inner function in parametrize_w_experiments is now dead code \u2014 its only call site was the removed else branch. It should be removed to avoid confusion.": 0.15988463163375854, "Boolean(normalizedDateRange) is always true because normalizeDateTimeParams returns an object (even an empty {}). This guard is a no-op \u2014 the query will fire whenever the feature flag is present, regardless of whether valid date params exist.": 0.9931723475456238, "Truthy check on cell conflates valid falsy ReactNode values (null, 0, '', false) with undefined. The return type React.ReactNode | undefined uses undefined to mean 'use default', so the check should be cell !== undefined.": 0.9185638427734375, "format_comment_subtitle is now dead code. The only call site was removed in this change (replaced by self.get_merged_pr_single_issue_template which doesn't use subtitle). Consider removing the method.": 0.1317078024148941, "attributes can be undefined on initial load because data (and previous) are undefined until the query resolves. Provide a TagCollection fallback to keep the return shape stable.": 0.7222155928611755, "hidden-xs hidden-sm is on the inner TimeSince but the wrapping TextOverflow div will still render as an empty flex item on small screens. Move the className to TextOverflow so the entire wrapper is hidden.": 0.8894514441490173, "pipeline.fetch_state('github_authenticated_user') can return None if the OAuth login step didn't execute properly. This would cause the comparison to always evaluate as a mismatch, returning a confusing USER_MISMATCH error instead of handling the missing state explicitly.": 0.003940541762858629, "Typo: 'segements' should be 'segments'.": 0.03020109236240387, "dedupedYAxes is a misleading name \u2014 it's now just [chart.yAxis], a single-element array with no deduplication. Consider simplifying this block to process chart.yAxis directly and renaming the variable.": 0.005600091069936752, "The new subscription results consumers are missing from the full mode. The full mode includes every other consumer defined in the file; omitting these four new consumers looks like an oversight.": 0.8809542655944824}